Looking for work that has a real impact on access to justice? Want to help make legal knowledge more accessible and create practical solutions that empower individuals across Canada? Through our flat-rate legal service plans tailored to the needs of our members, we provide accessible legal support to more than 300,000 Canadians.
In this role, you'll provide personalized legal consultations, helping clients understand their rights, obligations, and options across a broad range of legal matters. You'll assess legal situations, deliver practical advice, develop tailored strategies, and guide clients through complex issues with confidence, while collaborating with a dedicated team committed to making legal services more accessible. Your Responsibilities
Provide personalized remote legal consultations in clear and accessible languages across various fields of law (residential leasing, real estate, immigration, administrative law, criminal law, university law, labor law, etc.);
Prepare cases for litigation: fact and legal analysis, evidence review, drafting procedures, and representation strategy;
Support the current team in representing clients before civil courts and administrative bodies in a variety of legal areas (university disciplinary committees, Landlord Tenant Board, Small Claims Court);
Analyze legal files and situations presented by clients to assess their rights, obligations, and options;
Advise clients throughout the legal process, clearly explaining the issues, next steps, and possible options;
Evaluate the chances of success of potential legal actions, and offer realistic and client-tailored solutions;
Rigorously track deadlines and procedural obligations;
Collaborate with the entire legal team to ensure a cohesive approach;
Stay current with legislative and regulatory changes in relevant areas of law;
Occasionally participate in hearings: meet with clients to prepare their testimony, present evidence, conduct examinations, present arguments, and negotiate settlements if needed.
Your Profile
Licensee as a lawyer from a Canadian Law Society for at least two (2) years;
Ability to manage a high volume of legal cases and prioritize effectively;
Demonstrates empathy and active listening with clients;
Communicates clearly and adapts messaging to different audiences;
Resourceful and solution-oriented;
A team player who encourages collaboration and supports colleagues;

Current and active MD Bar membership in good standing;
Up to 7 years’ litigation experience preferred, preferably in MD but open to all candidates with relevant skills; Opportunities exist for more experienced candidates and can be found via another job posting.
Superior written and oral communications skills;
Strong organization and attention to detail;
Ability to multitask in a fast-paced environment;
Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint) and LexisNexis;
Familiarity with Case/File Management systems;

Competitive salary for the entry level to mid-level litigation attorney is in the range of $85,000 – $120,000 and is commensurate upon experience;
The ability to earn addition compensation through productivity and discretionary bonuses;
Mentorship, training and a clear path to leadership;
